  "notes": [
   "The booklet has no inventory page with Element IDs (page 2 only lists other sets). Part types use common LEGO design numbers where I recognised the piece (3020, 3022, 3003, 3001, 3039, 3069) and 'lego-unknown-*' placeholders for pieces I could not identify.",
   "Piece identities, counts and exact stud placement were estimated from small step pictures. In particular, the pink seat parts, the white body bricks, the front body piece and the wheel and wheel-holder arrangement are approximate.",
   "Colour names are read from the pictures. The teal piece is recorded as 'medium azure'.",
   "Wheels are shown with grey tyres in the final picture. The wheel holders are on the black base plates in step 1, and the wheels are fitted in steps 5-8, so each wheel is attached to a holder on the nearest base plate.",
   "Emma is built as four parts (hair, head, torso, skirt/legs) and seated in the car in step 8. Her legs are attached to a seat piece (b4)."
  ]
